spans.s:
pauṃs-na, a. human;
 fit for a man;
 🞄n. manliness, manhood.

paúṃs-ya, a. manly, peculiar to men;
 🞄n. manliness;
 manly power, courage, or deed: 🞄pl. hosts of men.

paunar-bhava, a. connected with 🞄a remarried woman;
 m. son of a remarried 🞄woman;
 -bhavika, a. (ī) relating to a second 🞄birth;
 -vasava, a. relating to the physician 🞄Punarvasu: w. yuvan, m. student of medicine;
 🞄-vācika, a. pleonastic, redundant.
